# TypeScript

```typescript
// ✅
interface FilterGamesOptions {
  lastN?: number;
}

const filterGames = (
  games: GameLog[],
  options: FilterGamesOptions = {},
): GameLog[] => {
  const { lastN } = options;
  // ...
};

type PlayerId = number;
```

```typescript
// ❌
type FilterGamesOptions = { lastN?: number }; // use interface for objects
function filterGames({ lastN }: FilterGamesOptions) {} // no destructure in params
catch (e: unknown) {} // no unknown/any
```

- Prefer small pure helpers; one level of abstraction in exported functions.
- Immutability: do not mutate input arrays/objects unless the API explicitly requires it.
